![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

When unpacking `INT4` nibbles, if the tensor has an odd number of elements, unpacking both nibbles of the last byte will result in one extra element. We should limit the unpacked elements to the exact expected count of the tensor.

```rust
            "INT4" | "I4" | "U4" => {
                let expected_elements = loc.shape.iter().product::<usize>();
                let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(expected_elements);
                for &byte in bytes {
                    let low = byte & 0x0F;
                    if out.len() < expected_elements {
                        out.push(low as f32);
                    }
                    let high = byte >> 4;
                    if out.len() < expected_elements {
                        out.push(high as f32);
                    }
                }
                Ok(out)
            }
```

![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

In `extract_token_embedding`, we should also limit the unpacked `INT4` elements to the exact `row_elements` count to avoid returning an extra element if `row_elements` is odd.

```rust
            "INT4" | "I4" | "U4" => {
                let mut out = Vec::with_capacity(row_elements);
                for &byte in bytes {
                    let low = byte & 0x0F;
                    if out.len() < row_elements {
                        out.push(low as f32);
                    }
                    let high = byte >> 4;
                    if out.len() < row_elements {
                        out.push(high as f32);
                    }
                }
                Ok(out)
            }
